<node id="CMS">
  <data key="d0">CMS</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">CMS stands for Content Management System, a platform for managing and organizing content.&lt;SEP&gt;CMS refers to a content management system that allows users to control and manage their site's content.&lt;SEP&gt;CMS stands for Content Management System, which is used to manage collection content.&lt;SEP&gt;CMS stands for Content Management System, which is a platform for managing and publishing digital content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a35c395eb2de6194b0d0b819cc25645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d8052bab145fa732f5fa1156e51a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0953e715dad6f364462f8aebf53207a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-134de6c869a1bdf0a400dfea307efdce</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762778651</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Collection View">
  <data key="d0">Collection View</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">The collection view is where items are displayed and can be reordered or hidden.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection view is a way to organize and display items in a collection, allowing for customization and filtering.&lt;SEP&gt;A collection view is a way to organize and display items in a collection within the CMS.&lt;SEP&gt;The collection view is a feature in Wix's CMS that allows users to manage and organize their collections.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a35c395eb2de6194b0d0b819cc25645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0f039145f41fa401d0e8e33a185f71a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4d8052bab145fa732f5fa1156e51a44&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-134de6c869a1bdf0a400dfea307efdce</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762778695</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Fields">
  <data key="d0">Fields</data>
  <data key="d1">concept</data>
  <data key="d2">Fields refer to the individual elements or columns within a collection view, which can be hidden, shown, or reordered.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a35c395eb2de6194b0d0b819cc25645d</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
  <data key="d5">1762778014</data>
  <data key="d6"></data>
</node>
<node id="Editor">
  <data key="d0">Editor</data>
  <data key="d1">location</data>
  <data key="d2">The editor is a tool or interface used for creating, modifying, and managing content within a platform or system.&lt;SEP&gt;The editor is another location where users can access and manage their collection content.</data>
  <data key="d3">chunk-a35c395eb2de6194b0d0b819cc25645d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0953e715dad6f364462f8aebf53207a</data>
  <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
